# ExaBGP qa/old/4.2/qa/ci/conf-ipself6 (ExaBGP 685f772e4e): .ci and .msg joined, options spelt option=
option=file:conf-ipself6.conf
option=allowed:the release announced 2a04:6d80::1/128 with next-hop self, which on this loopback session is ::1, the peer's own address and not a global address; RFC 4271 Section 5.1.3 says "A route originated by a BGP speaker SHALL NOT be advertised to a peer using an address of that peer as NEXT_HOP", and RFC 2545 Section 3 says the speaker "shall advertise to its peer in the Network Address of Next Hop field the global IPv6 address of the next hop", so ze refuses the next hop and sends no route
